<newsitem itemid="172305" id="root" date="1996-11-07" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Nedcor year shr, div surges.</title>
<headline>Nedcor year shr, div surges.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    502	     vs 386</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    155	     vs 119</p>
<p>    Net income after tax     1,082	   vs 782</p>
<p>    Net interest income	2,981	   vs 2,430</p>
<p>    Non interest revenue     2,004	   vs 1,614</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 333	     vs 233</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			1,592	   vs 1,205</p>
<p>    Tax			    510	     vs 423</p>
<p>Full name: Nedcor Ltd (banking)</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters expected earnings to rise to between 477 and 480 cents with consensus pegged at 478.6 cents. They forecast a dividend of 149 cents.</p>
<p>Directors said they would issue capitalisation shares, the terms of which would be announced around November 13.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
